  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture legacy-written list and draft samples on a Mac so that LOT-067's importer can be checked against the formats that the legacy app actually writes. The tests in PR #703 currently construct samples from the legacy shapes.\n\n### Scope\n\nUsing synthetic data, generate samples of:\n\n- `blackListDico.plist`\n- `whiteList.plist`\n- `blackList.plist` (v0)\n- `brouillon`\n- `reply_active_drafts_by_topic_v1`\n\nRecord the legacy revision, how each sample was produced, and where each format is stored. Include empty and typical samples where the legacy app can produce them.\n\nUse the synthetic-data and review safeguards from #347 and `docs/FIXTURES.md`. Do not publish real account data, cookies, tokens, or other private information.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The legacy app generated samples for each listed format, or the issue records why a sample could not be generated.\n- [ ] The samples contain synthetic data only and receive an independent privacy review before publication.\n- [ ] The capture PR records the provenance and storage location of each sample.\n- [ ] The capture PR adds the samples and any required manifest entries, and checks the applicable LOT-067 importer against them.\n\n### Context\n\n- LOT-067: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/92\n- Importer PR: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/703\n- Earlier small-store capture and safeguards: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/347\n- Requester: @francoisgn\n- Report: https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/368",
